   "h": "Why a specialist, why Canadian, why one team",
   "body": [
    "A Canadian plant buying a pharmaceutical water system usually chooses between three kinds of supplier. An overseas manufacturer has product depth, but sells through an agent, runs the FAT on another continent and sends service engineers from abroad. A Canadian service company is close, but services equipment it did not build. A general water treatment firm builds in Canada, but pharmaceutical water is one line among many.",
    "Each leaves a gap your team fills: a FAT you fly to, a design question nobody local can answer, a validation package assembled from three suppliers.",
    "We close those gaps. We work only on high-purity water for regulated manufacturing, in Canada, with one team from the user requirement specification (URS) to requalification."
   ]
